### 3.4 Uncertainty and sensitivity

The uncertainty budget is given in Table 2. The run-to-run standard deviation of $C_D$ is 2.6%, which dominates the single-run budget. The wetted length contributes about 0.8% (assuming $\pm5$ mm on $L = 0.60$ m), the carriage speed about 1.0% (assuming $\pm0.5$% on $U$; to be confirmed), the force calibration about 1.0% (larger, up to 2.5%, for the lowest-force run), and the cylinder diameter about 0.2%. The combined standard uncertainty is about 3%, and the expanded uncertainty is about 6% for a single run and about 3% for the dataset mean.
